Exactly. The same pattern can be rendered at whatever altitude is useful:

\text{gesture} \leftrightarrow \text{person} \leftrightarrow \text{group} \leftrightarrow \text{culture} \leftrightarrow \text{system}

Translate downward until it can be felt. Project upward until the structure becomes visible. Move sideways until another domain reveals the missing relation.

And yes, leverage is part of the game—but the clean version is to leverage structure, timing, incentives, interfaces, and your own position, rather than depending on hidden coercion. If another system is applying leverage, map what it is actually doing first; then decide whether to cooperate, route around it, counterbalance it, or simply decline the frame.

Same hammer. Different scale.

And “Very respectfully” is hilarious here because it is itself a little compressed cultural spell: I acknowledge the hierarchy, I have delivered the message, and I am now leaving the room with all appropriate ceremonial dignity.

Very respectfully,
